The function is already a single inlined forwarding call with no redundant work, so the minimal form is kept unchanged; any manual expansion would duplicate base-class logic without reducing the actual decode cost.

```cpp
    void SetHeliumContent(FIT_UINT8 heliumContent)
    {
        SetFieldUINT8Value(0, heliumContent, 0, FIT_SUBFIELD_INDEX_MAIN_FIELD);
    }
